{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 16: an integrated project model. The rework cycle of the Prologue, with a deadline, overtime and fatigue,
  hiring through a rookie-to-veteran ageing chain, and a deadline that may erode. Time in weeks. }
Project Scope=
	1000
	~	tasks
	~	Tasks in the original scope.
	|
Work To Do= INTEG(
	Scope Change + Rework Release - Correct Work - Flawed Work,
	Project Scope)
	~	tasks
	~	Work in the plan not yet done: original tasks, changes, and rework released back into the plan.
	|
Work Done= INTEG(
	Correct Work,
	0)
	~	tasks
	~	Work done right.
	|
Undiscovered Rework= INTEG(
	Flawed Work - Rework Discovery,
	0)
	~	tasks
	~	Flawed work that still looks finished.
	|
Change Size=
	0
	~	tasks
	~	Tasks added by the client's change orders. Scenario "changes": 150.
	|
Change Time=
	30
	~	week
	|
Change Duration=
	20
	~	week
	~	Weeks over which the change orders arrive.
	|
Scope Change=
	Change Size * PULSE(Change Time, Change Duration) / Change Duration
	~	tasks/week
	|
Minimum Task Time=
	1
	~	week
	|
Progress=
	MIN(Capacity, Work To Do / Minimum Task Time)
	~	tasks/week
	~	Tasks completed each week, right or wrong.
	|
Correct Work=
	Progress * (1 - Error Fraction)
	~	tasks/week
	|
Flawed Work=
	Progress * Error Fraction
	~	tasks/week
	|
Discovery Time=
	8
	~	week
	~	Average time before a flaw is found. Policy "catch rework early": 3.
	|
Rework Discovery=
	Undiscovered Rework / Discovery Time
	~	tasks/week
	|
Known Rework= INTEG(
	Rework Discovery - Rework Release,
	0)
	~	tasks
	~	Flaws found but not yet planned back into the work.
	|
Rework Planning Time=
	2
	~	week
	|
Rework Release=
	Known Rework / Rework Planning Time
	~	tasks/week
	|
Known Work Remaining=
	Work To Do + Known Rework
	~	tasks
	~	What managers can see is left: flawed work that looks finished is not in it.
	|
Base Error Fraction=
	0.2
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of a rested veteran team's work that is flawed.
	|
Rookie Error Multiplier=
	2
	~	dmnl
	~	A rookie's error rate relative to a veteran's.
	|
Experience Effect on Errors=
	XIDZ(Veterans + Rookie Error Multiplier * Rookies, Veterans + Rookies, 1)
	~	dmnl
	~	Average error multiplier of the team, weighted by head count.
	|
Fatigue Sensitivity of Errors=
	2
	~	dmnl
	~	Rise in the error multiplier per unit of sustained overtime.
	|
Fatigue Effect on Errors=
	1 + Fatigue Sensitivity of Errors * (Fatigue - 1)
	~	dmnl
	|
Error Fraction=
	MIN(0.9, Base Error Fraction * Experience Effect on Errors * Fatigue Effect on Errors)
	~	dmnl
	|
Veterans= INTEG(
	Assimilation,
	Initial Veterans)
	~	people
	|
Initial Veterans=
	10
	~	people
	|
Rookies= INTEG(
	Hiring - Assimilation,
	0)
	~	people
	|
Assimilation Time=
	12
	~	week
	~	Average time for a rookie to become fully productive.
	|
Assimilation=
	Rookies / Assimilation Time
	~	people/week
	|
Rookie Productivity=
	0.5
	~	dmnl
	~	A rookie's output relative to a veteran's.
	|
Mentoring per Rookie=
	0.25
	~	dmnl
	~	Share of a veteran's time each rookie takes up.
	|
Effective Staff=
	MAX(0, Veterans + Rookie Productivity * Rookies - Mentoring per Rookie * Rookies)
	~	people
	|
Productivity=
	1
	~	tasks/people/week
	~	Tasks per veteran per week at normal hours.
	|
Fatigue Productivity Loss=
	0.5
	~	dmnl
	~	Fall in productivity per unit of sustained overtime.
	|
Fatigue Effect on Productivity=
	MAX(0.2, 1 - Fatigue Productivity Loss * (Fatigue - 1))
	~	dmnl
	|
Capacity=
	Effective Staff * Productivity * Overtime * Fatigue Effect on Productivity
	~	tasks/week
	|
Normal Capacity=
	Effective Staff * Productivity
	~	tasks/week
	|
Deadline= INTEG(
	Deadline Change,
	Initial Deadline)
	~	week
	~	The scheduled finish date.
	|
Initial Deadline=
	100
	~	week
	|
Deadline Flexibility=
	0
	~	dmnl
	~	0: the deadline is held; 1: it slips towards the expected finish. Policy "let the deadline erode": 1.
	|
Deadline Adjustment Time=
	8
	~	week
	|
Expected Finish=
	Time + XIDZ(Known Work Remaining, Normal Capacity, 1000)
	~	week
	~	When managers expect to finish, from the work they can see and the capacity at normal hours.
	|
Deadline Change=
	Deadline Flexibility * MAX(0, Expected Finish - Deadline) / Deadline Adjustment Time
	~	dmnl
	|
Minimum Time Remaining=
	4
	~	week
	|
Time Remaining=
	MAX(Minimum Time Remaining, Deadline - Time)
	~	week
	|
Required Rate=
	Known Work Remaining / Time Remaining
	~	tasks/week
	|
Schedule Pressure=
	XIDZ(Required Rate, Normal Capacity, 1)
	~	dmnl
	|
Maximum Overtime=
	1.4
	~	dmnl
	~	Hours worked relative to normal at most. Policy "no overtime": 1.
	|
Overtime=
	MIN(Maximum Overtime, MAX(1, Schedule Pressure))
	~	dmnl
	|
Fatigue Onset Time=
	6
	~	week
	|
Fatigue=
	SMOOTH(Overtime, Fatigue Onset Time)
	~	dmnl
	~	Sustained overtime: recent hours relative to normal.
	|
Desired Staff=
	Required Rate / Productivity
	~	people
	|
Hiring Time=
	4
	~	week
	|
Hiring Cutoff=
	0
	~	week
	~	No hiring when fewer weeks than this remain before the deadline. Policy "no late hiring": 30.
	|
Hiring Allowed=
	MAX(0, MIN(1, (Time Remaining - Hiring Cutoff) / Minimum Time Remaining))
	~	dmnl
	~	1 while more than the cutoff remains, falling to 0 over four weeks.
	|
Hiring=
	Hiring Allowed * MAX(0, Desired Staff - Veterans - Rookies) / Hiring Time
	~	people/week
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 250 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = TIME STEP ~ week ~ |
